WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

NOTE
On-screen text of the 50-second overview film, timed to the scenes. The film carries an audio track; its content has not been transcribed here. Source of all figures: Humanitarian Reset Stocktake (draft), October 2026.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
IASC. The Humanitarian Reset.
Stocktake, October 2026.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The Humanitarian Reset:
Define, Deliver, Devolve, Defend.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Define. 62% of people assisted were in severity 4–5 areas:
36% in 2024, 43% in 2025, 62% in 2026.

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Define. 75% of Humanitarian Needs
and Response Plans include transition plans.

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Deliver. 66 million people reached, including 41 million
in the most severe locations, by October 2026.

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Deliver. $4.53 billion in country-based pooled funds.
79% of operations have started or completed cluster simplification.

7
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Devolve. Broader local participation.
Stronger country-level accountability.

8
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Defend. Principled humanitarian action.
International humanitarian law. Human rights.

9
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Progress is real but uneven.

10
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.050
IASC, Inter-Agency Standing Committee.
www.interagencystandingcommittee.org
